<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blantyre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blantyre is the main commercial city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shire-highlands">Shire Highlands</a> of the south. It was founded in 1876 as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-scotland">Church of Scotland</a> mission and named after the Scottish birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a>. The mission and the trading posts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-lakes-company">African Lakes Company</a> drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> into the region and led to the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blantyre.jpg" alt="Blantyre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SMuyila · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blantyre_City.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
